{
  "about": "Every view returns the same things in the core as in Grafeo (editor spec §7: views_agree_with_grafeo). Small notes, each a graph's data blocks and its views, every view a named query block of the note; for each view, the view its query is read as (spec), the things it returns (things, sorted by id), and, as the core draws them, the links shown with them (from TYPE to, in the core's order), the names asked for that are not there (missing) and a walked path's steps in order (walk). left_out names the blocks the reader refuses, which the core leaves out of its drawing and Grafeo is never given. Then queries outside the view profile, each with the reason the core gives and the shape it is nearest to. Held to the core by packages/core/test/view-parity.test.js, and to Grafeo by tests/test_view_parity.py.",
  "allowed": "A view query has one of five shapes: a hand-picked set of things, everything near a thing, how one thing reaches another, only some kinds, a walked path",
